{"repositoryId":1120340155,"availability":"available","full":"cuihairu/soar","name":"soar","description":"Cross-platform open source media player built with FFmpeg, SDL2 and libass (C++17).","category":"Other","language":"C++","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-12-21T01:58:31Z","updated":"2026-10-15T10:31:24Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cuihairu.github.io/soar/","topics":["cmake","cpp","cpp17","cross-platform","desktop-application","ffmpeg","http-cache","imgui","media-player","sdl2","subtitles","vcpkg","video-player"],"demo":"https://cuihairu.github.io/soar/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.764Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.764Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.764Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.764Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Soar is an open-source C++17 media player built on FFmpeg + SDL2: it wraps a core playback abstraction plus a desktop UI, delegates demuxing and decoding to FFmpeg, and treats \"playing every format you can think of\" as a long-term goal.","We kept hitting the same pitfalls in past player projects: playback cores entangled with UI, dependency licenses blocking distribution, and a core locked to one platform framework just when we wanted to reuse it on mobile. Soar turns these three lessons into design constraints."],"features":["Media input: local files, multiple files queued (soar … — the first plays, the rest queue), network stream URLs (http(s)/HLS/DASH/RTSP and every other protocol FFmpeg supports), .torrent files and magnet: links; failure…","Playback control: play / pause / stop / seek / rate / volume and mute;","Playlist: N/Shift+N for next/previous (out-of-range shows a Toast instead of wrapping), auto-advance on natural end (stops at Ended on the last item; Space replays), P overlay with click-to-play and x to remove, Loop…","Media library: watch folders (recursively scanned, missing files pruned; entries opened directly — URLs, files outside every watched folder — are never pruned), per-source play history with resume (a position past 5 s…","Screenshots and A-B loop: S saves the most recently presented frame as screenshot.png; L sets a three-step loop (set A → set B → clear, jumps back at EOF, cleared by a manual seek);"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cuihairu/soar/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"8d285906bdfa94c86f973b0453be59f2cc35fc43cc8ca958992750337acedf63","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.845Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.845Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Soar is an open-source C++17 media player built on FFmpeg + SDL2: it wraps a core playback abstraction plus a desktop UI, delegates demuxing and decoding to FFmpeg, and treats \"playing every format you can think of\" as a long-term goal.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cuihairu/soar/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"Subtitle rendering: built-in ASS/SSA rendered with libass styling (fonts/colors/positioning/effects follow the script; container-attached fonts are used as-is), external .ass/.ssa rendered with the same styling, external SRT/WebVTT rendered on the same canvas with the repository default style (builds without libass degrade to plain text), built-in SRT/WebVTT text subtitles…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cuihairu/soar/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"8d285906bdfa94c86f973b0453be59f2cc35fc43cc8ca958992750337acedf63","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cuihairu/soar/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.846Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-15T10:31:24Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cuihairu/soar/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:39.848Z","hash":"8d285906bdfa94c86f973b0453be59f2cc35fc43cc8ca958992750337acedf63","originalBytes":23812,"storedBytes":23812,"truncated":false,